      "content": "To address partner resistance, you must first demonstrate the tangible financial risk of SMS interception by highlighting how the \"hassle\" is actually a premium insurance policy against data leaks. Frame the temporary day-one inconvenience as a one-time friction point for permanent security gains, arguing that the once-a-login key tap is infinitely safer and faster than waiting for and verifying potentially scammed texts. Provide a detailed, step-by-step quick-start guide with physical hints like key clip cases to reduce perceived effort, showing them exactly how much faster the process feels compared to searching for a phone in a meeting. Ultimately, anchor the conversation on liability: sound practice dictates that protecting client confidentiality is worth the minor administrative adjustment they will make today to prevent costly breaches tomorrow.",
